      "side": 1,
      "message": "The issue is that adding `#ifdef TEST_BUILD` means that the code coverage will never show the call to charger_current_battery_params() has covered by tests.\n\nThere are 2 approaches you could take here:\n\n1. Modify the `charger_current_battery_params()` prototype to create an inline version when the charger task isn\u0027t available.\n```\n#ifdef HAS_TASK_CHARGER\nconst struct batt_params *charger_current_battery_params(void);\n#else\ninline const struct batt_params *charger_current_battery_params(void)\n{\n   /* Return the battery_get_params() pointer */\n}\n#endif\n```\n\n2. In the test code, create a fake for `charger_current_battery_params()` that just returns the `battery_get_params()` pointer.  This is effectively the same thing as option 1, but it makes it explicit that only test code should be referencing the charger code without a charger task.\n\nOption 2 is preferred, but requires some analysis to see if any of the legacy tests need to also create the fake `charger_current_battery_params()`.\n\nI\u0027m okay with option 1.",
